# Diagnostics & graph rules

- Read `knowledge/context/modules/diagnostics.md` and `knowledge/flows/FLOW-diagnose.md` before editing.
- Label ranking as heuristic/case-based — never as calibrated fault probabilities or conflict F1.
- Preserve citation validation; never weaken it for demos.
- Fail loud when Groq is unavailable and no valid diag cache exists (controlled 503).
- Coordinate any diagnose JSON field rename with Shahmeer; record a DEC if the contract changes.
- Prefer bounded Neo4j queries; no fabricated graph edges.
- After changes: update the diagnostics module note and FLOW-diagnose dependency graph if edges changed.
